+/*
+ * BMP 103: diagnostics for a transport that cannot report a lost access.
+ *
+ * ENABLE_DEBUG is 0 on the embedded builds, so every DEBUG_WARN() in this file compiles to
+ * nothing on the probe - the probe's own log sink is Logger(), and it is the channel the SDI
+ * tap's traces use. These lines are only emitted while the memory path is instrumented
+ * (`mon memlog on`, bmp_mem_log_enabled, riscv_fault.md §9), because a log write during a GDB
+ * reply is exactly what §9 had to move behind that switch; the readable-but-silent alternative
+ * for the same numbers is `mon riscv_confirm`, which reads the counters below.
+ */
